            "finalAnswer": "I now have the complete trace. Here's the flow:\n\n## The React component: `StaticCanvas`\n\n`packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx` — a `React.memo`-wrapped component. In its `useEffect`, on every re-render (governed by the custom `areEqual` comparator watching `sceneNonce`, `elementsMap`, `visibleElements`, etc.) it calls:\n\n```ts\nrenderStaticScene({ canvas, rc: props.rc, scale, elementsMap, allElementsMap, visibleElements, appState, renderConfig }, isRenderThrottlingEnabled())\n```\n\n`renderStaticScene` (`packages/excalidraw/renderer/staticScene.ts:470`) either calls the RAF-throttled wrapper or the internal `_renderStaticScene` directly, which iterates `visibleElements` and calls `renderElement(...)` (`packages/excalidraw/renderer/renderElement.ts:698`) for each one.\n\n## Where the roughjs shape comes from\n\nInside `renderElement`, for drawable types (`rectangle`, `diamond`, `ellipse`, `line`, `arrow`, `image`, `text`, `iframe`, `embeddable`, `freedraw`), it first calls:\n\n```ts\nShapeCache.generateElementShape(element, renderConfig)\n```\n\n(`packages/excalidraw/scene/ShapeCache.ts:47`). `ShapeCache` is a `WeakMap<ExcalidrawElement, ElementShape>` keyed by element reference — it checks `ShapeCache.get(element)`; if already cached (and not exporting), it returns the cached `Drawable`/shape immediately. Otherwise it calls `_generateElementShape(element, ShapeCache.rg, renderConfig)` in `packages/excalidraw/scene/Shape.ts:306`, which uses a shared `RoughGenerator` instance (`ShapeCache.rg = new RoughGenerator()`) to build the actual roughjs primitives — e.g. `generator.rectangle(...)`, `generator.ellipse(...)`, `generator.path(...)`, `generator.curve(...)` depending on element type — then caches the result via `ShapeCache.cache.set(element, shape)`.\n\nFinally, `renderElement` calls `drawElementOnCanvas(element, rc, context, renderConfig, appState)` (`renderElement.ts:383`), which does `rc.draw(ShapeCache.get(element)!)` using the `RoughCanvas` instance (`rc`, from `roughjs/bin/canvas`) passed down all the way from `StaticCanvas`'s props to actually paint the cached roughjs `Drawable` onto the `CanvasRenderingContext2D`.\n\nSo the pipeline is: **`StaticCanvas` (React component) → `renderStaticScene`/`_renderStaticScene` → `renderElement` per element → `ShapeCache.generateElementShape` (generates via `Shape.ts`'s `_generateElementShape` + a shared `RoughGenerator`, caching in a `WeakMap`) → `drawElementOnCanvas` → `rc.draw(...)`** onto the canvas context.",
